an style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Content-Length: 0 Content-Range: bytes */&lt;total&gt;</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">308 Resume Incomplete with Range header indicating authoritative byte boundary; resume streaming at high + 1.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Chunk sizing represents a critical engineering parameter. Google mandates that all resumable chunks must be exact multiples of 256 KB (262,144 bytes), with the exception of the final closing chunk. The engine enforces an operational chunk size of 16 MB (16 \times 1024 \times 1024 = 16,777,216 bytes). This size reduces HTTP request overhead on high-speed uplinks while bounding memory allocation and limiting re-transmission penalties to a single 16 MB segment if a TCP stream drops.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">If a network timeout, socket hangup, or 5xx platform error occurs during transmission, the client halts streaming immediately. Rather than restarting from byte zero, the engine executes recovery: it issues an empty PUT request with Content-Range: bytes[span_60](start_span)[span_60](end_span)[span_101](start_span)[span_101](end_span) */&lt;total_bytes&gt;. The response dictates the recovery pathway:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_1-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">If the server responds with HTTP 308 (Resume Incomplete) and a Range: bytes=0-33554431 header, the engine verifies that 32 MB have been committed, increments the pointer to byte 33,554,432, updates SQLite, and streams the subsequent chunk.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">If the server responds with HTTP 200 or 201, the entire file was successfully committed prior to connection loss; the engine parses the video JSON and bypasses re-upload.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">If the server returns HTTP 404 (Not Found), the session URI has expired or been purged from Google's ingestion caches. The engine clears the stale URI from the database and initializes a clean resumable session.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS upload_sessions (<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;publish_attempt_id TEXT PRIMARY K[span_61](start_span)[span_61](end_span)[span_102](start_span)[span_102](end_span)EY,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;project_video_id TEXT NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;artifact_id TEXT NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;channel_id TEXT NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;session_uri TEXT,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;youtube_video_id TEXT,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;total_bytes INTEGER NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;bytes_uploaded INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;chunk_size INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 16777216,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;sta[span_62](start_span)[span_62](end_span)[span_103](start_span)[span_103](end_span)tus TEXT NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;http_status_code INTEGER,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;last_error TEXT,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;expires_at TIMESTAMP,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;updated_at TIMESTAMP [span_63](start_span)[span_63](end_span)[span_104](start_span)[span_104](end_span)DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP<br>);<br><br>CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_upload_sessions_project ON upload_sessions(project_video_id)[span_64](start_span)[span_64](end_span)[span_105](start_span)[span_105](end_span);<br>CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_upload_sessions_status ON upload_sessions(status);<br></span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Authentication &amp; Credential Architecture</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Autonomous publishing requires a secure credential lifecycle capable of authenticating against YouTube channels without interactive human prompts during production runs. Google Cloud Service Accounts are unsupported for uploading videos to standard creator channels or Brand Accounts. Attempting to authorize videos.insert using a Service Account returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized or HTTP 403 Forbidden with serviceNotAvailable or insufficientPermissions errors. Only Content Partners utilizing YouTube CMS with the onBehalfOfContentOwner parameter can route uploads through Service Accounts.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;OAUTH 2.0 CREDENTIAL LIFECYCLE &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp;[One-Time Interactive Bootstrap] &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp;Operator CLI -&gt; Generate Consent URL -&gt; Web Auth -&gt; Authorization Code Callback -&gt; Exchange for Refresh Token &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â”‚ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â–¼ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp;[Secure Vault Storage] &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp;Encrypt Refresh Token via AES-256-GCM (ENGINE_VAULT_KEY) -&gt; Commit to SQLite channel_credentials Table &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â”‚ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â–¼ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp;[Autonomous Runtime Hydration] &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp;Read Encrypted Record -&gt; Decrypt Token -&gt; Evaluate Expiration Window (Now + 300 Seconds) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â”œâ”€â”€ [Token Valid] â”€â”€â”€&gt; Issue API Calls with Bearer Token in HTTP Authorization Header &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â””â”€â”€ [Token Expiring] &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â”‚ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â–¼ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp;[Proactive Token Rotation] &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp;POST https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token (grant_type=refresh_token) -&gt; Cache New Access Token (3600s Lifespan) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+<br></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Consequently, the autonomous engine standardizes on OAuth 2.0 User Credentials configured for offline access (access_type=offline, prompt=consent). This workflow generates a long-lived refresh token alongside a standard 3,600-second access token.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Two specific authorization scopes are required:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_2-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.upload: Provides explicit authorization to register resumable upload sessions and stream video media.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.force-ssl: Provides authorization to mutate video metadata, set custom thumbnails, insert captions, and manage playlist memberships. Broad scopes like https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube must be avoided under the principle of least privilege.</span></li></ul><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Token lifecycle management is subject to strict operational security rules:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_3-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Seven-Day Testing Expiration: If a Google Cloud project remains in the "Testing" publishing status, refresh tokens expire automatically after seven days (168 hours). For uninterrupted autonomous operation, the Google Cloud project must be transitioned to "In Production" status within the Google Cloud Console, or configured under an internal Google Workspace organization.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Zero-Leak Credential Policy: Client secrets, refresh tokens, and access tokens must never appear in LLM prompts, runtime logs, terminal outputs, version-controlled files, or unencrypted database tables. Credentials reside in an encrypted vault: on local developer machines, tokens map to OS keychains (Secret Service on Linux, Keychain on macOS); in headless production environments, tokens are stored in SQLite encrypted using AES-256-GCM, with the vault key injected via ENGINE_VAULT_KEY.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Proactive Token Refresh: The engine checks token validity prior to dispatching any API call. If the current access token expires within 300 seconds, the runtime dispatches a refresh request to https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token using the client credentials and refresh token.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS channel_credentials (<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;channel_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;account_email TEXT NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;encrypted_refresh_token BLOB NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;token_iv BLOB NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;token_tag BLOB NOT NULL,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;token_expiry TIMESTAMP,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;is_active INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;reauth_required INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;last_refreshed_at TIMESTAMP,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP<br>);<br></span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Publishing State Machine</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The publishing state machine decouples internal workflow orchestration from observable YouTube API states. Internal st