dpoint: POST https://www.googleapis.com/upload/you[span_73](start_span)[span_73](end_span)[span_114](start_span)[span_114](end_span)tube/v3/thumbnails/set?videoId={VIDEO_ID}.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Platform requirements and operational constraints include:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_5-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Format and Dimensions: Supported formats include JPG, PNG, GIF, and BMP. Thumbnails must maintain a 16:9 aspect ratio, with a minimum resolution of 640x360 pixels and a recommended standard resolution of 1280x720 pixels.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">File Size Constraints: While YouTube Data API documentation notes thumbnail upload limits up to 50 MB, internal project policy limits thumbnails to \le 2 MB. This avoids edge timeouts and accelerates image processing.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Verified Account Requirement: The target channel must possess verified status (phone verification enabled in YouTube Studio). If unverified, the endpoint returns an HTTP 403 Forbidden error with reason thumbnailUploadDisabled.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Mutation Behavior: Invoking thumbnails.set immediately replaces any existing thumbnail, whether auto-generated by the platform or previously uploaded.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Quota Cost: Exactly 50 units from the general quota pool.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Verification: Successful upload returns a Thumbnail[span_367](start_span)[span_367](end_span)[span_375](start_span)[span_375](end_span)[span_383](start_span)[span_383](end_span)SetResponse containing URLs for default, medium, and high variants. The engine executes a lightweight HTTP HEAD request against the returned high-resolution URL to confirm CDN propagation.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Caption Delivery</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Subtitles can be delivered as burned-in open captions or discrete closed caption tracks via the API: POST https://www.googleapis.com/upload/youtube/v3/captions?part=[span_201](start_span)[span_201](end_span)snippet.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">| Delivery Dimension | Burned-In Open Captions | Discrete API Caption Tracks | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | API Quota Consumption | 0 API units (Rendered via FFmpeg) | 400 general units per track | | Viewer Control | Always visible; cannot be disabled | Toggleable; customizable appearance | | Algorithmic Indexing | Not indexed by search crawlers | Fully indexed by YouTube search | | Platform Styling | Fixed typography across all devices | Subject to viewer client settings | | Format Requirements | Video pixel data | Timed SRT, VTT, TTML, SCC, or SBV | | Short-Form Suitability | Highly effective for vertical Shorts | Poorly suited for rapid short-form viewing | | Long-Form Suitability | Obtrusive on long documentaries | Preferred standard for accessibility |</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Technical constraints governing API caption delivery include:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_6-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Deprecation of Untimed Transcripts: Effective April 12, 2024, the YouTube Data API deprecated the sync parameter, which previously permitted uploading raw transcript text for server-side alignment. All programmatic caption uploads must include synchronized timecodes.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Quota Expense: Each caption track insertion consumes 400 units from the general quota pool. Uploading three language tracks alongside a video burns 1,200 units (12% of the daily general budget).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Strategic Policy: Burned-in captions are mandatory for vertical Shorts, consuming zero quota and guaranteeing visual consistency. Flagship long-form videos utilize discrete WebVTT tracks uploaded via the API to maximize accessibility and search indexing.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding