000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Profile Isolation: Each profile encapsulates channel identity (channel_id), encrypted credential references, quota limits, metadata defaults, and default playlist bindings.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Multi-Tenant Quota Fair-Share: The Google Cloud project's default allocation of 100 uploads per day is shared across all authenticated channels. The orchestrator enforces per-channel daily caps, preventing high-frequency channels from starving lower-volume channels of upload quota.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">YouTube CMS Content Partner Support: For enterprise accounts, the publisher supports onBehalfOfContentOwner and onBehalfOfContentOwnerChannel parameters. This allows centralized authentication using a CMS identity to manage multiple client channels without requiring separate OAuth consent flows per channel.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Golden Path Recommendation: The initial deployment implements multi-channel schema abstracti