END. The foundational SDK for YouTube Data API v3 integration.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Licensing, Terms of Service, and Policy Considerations</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Autonomous publishing workflows are subject to platform and legal compliance constraints:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_b-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Google APIs Terms of Service &amp; Developer Policies: Automated uploads via the official YouTube Data API v3 are permitted provided applications comply with quota allocations, avoid scraping, and maintain accurate metadata. Simulating user interactions via browser automation to bypass API limitations violates Section III.E of the Developer Policies.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Mandatory Developer Compliance Audit: Google requires projects created after July 28, 2020, to complete an API compliance audit before enabling public uploads. Without audit approval, all programmatic uploads are restricted to private viewing mode. Autonomous public distribution requires completing this audit.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Synthetic Media Mandates: Under platform policies updated October 30, 2024, creators must disclose realistic altered or AI-generated media. Setting status.containsSyntheticMedia: true is mandatory for synthetic content; failing to disclose AI media risks strikes or API termination.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Child Online Privacy Protection: YouTube requires explicit audience declarations (status.selfDeclaredMadeForKids) on every video to comply with COPPA regulations.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Open-Source Dependencies: The primary client libraries (google-api-python-client, google-auth, httpx) are distributed under Apache 2.0 and BSD licenses, permitting commercial integration within proprietary architectures.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.