bsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp;Uploads custom thumbnail (thumbnails.set, 50 units) and inserts video into target playlists (50 units). &nbsp;|<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â”‚ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â–¼ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp;[Dual-Track Verification] &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp;Validates metadata and privacy status via API; confirms public CDN playback via unauthenticated HTTP GET.|<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â”‚ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; â–¼ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp;[Audit Finalization &amp; Handoff] &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp;Appends transaction to publish_audit_ledger; emits telemetry manifest to downstream analytics subsystem. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>+-------------[span_345](start_span)[span_345](end_span)[span_348](start_span)[span_348](end_span)[span_351](start_span)[span_351](end_span)------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+<br></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The system operates across five coordinated stages:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_list_11-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Manifest Compilation &amp; Preflight Verification: Upstream rendering engines generate media artifacts and sign a PublishPackage JSON manifest. The pre-publish validator confirms file existence, computes SHA-256 digests, ensures title and description lengths meet platform bounds, verifies that scheduled videos are initialized as private, and validates that the synthetic media disclosure flag is explicitly set.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Orchestration &amp; Token Hydration: The orchestrator claims an exclusive transaction lock on project_video_id in SQLite. It resolves the channel profile, queries the credential vault, decrypts the OAuth refresh token using AES-256-GCM, and acquires a fresh bearer access token from Google identity servers.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Quota Verification &amp; Session Initiation: The quota dispatcher consults the local SQLite ledger to confirm that the project's 100-upload and 10,000-general-unit daily budgets have not been exhausted. It dispatches a session initiation POST request to YouTube's resumable upload endpoint, extracts the session URI from the Location response header, and commits the URI and generated youtube_video_id to SQLite.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Chunked Ingestion &amp; Failure Recovery: The upload engine streams the video file in 16 MB chunks, updating SQLite with the byte offset confirmed by YouTube's HTTP 308 responses. If a connection drops, it halts, issues an empty PUT status query, extracts the platform's confirmed byte range, and resumes streaming from that offset.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Processing Reconciliation &amp; Telemetry Handoff: Once binary ingestion yields HTTP 200/201, the engine polls videos.list using exponential backoff. When processingDetails.processingStatus reaches succeeded, the asset binder uploads the custom thumbnail and assigns playlists. The engine verifies that observed platform states match declared metadata, runs a public edge HTTP check against the watch URL, appends a final record to publish_audit_ledger, and emits the permanent youtube_video_id to the downstream analytics subsystem.</span></li></ol><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Autonomous delivery succeeds only when platform constraints, cryptographic verification, and defensive network protocols operate in concert. By enforcing strict local preflight checks, treating the YouTube API as an asynchronous state machine rather than a synchronous storage layer, and decoupling binary ingestion from post-upload state reconciliation, this architecture guarantees that content delivery remains deterministic, resilient to network disruptions, fully compliant with platform policies, and traceable across the operational lifecycle.</span></p><h4 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Works cited</span></h4><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">1. YouTube API Pricing 2026: Quota, Upload Limits, Real Costs, https://www.outstand.so/blog/youtube-api-pricing-quota 2. Revision History | YouTube Data API - Google for Developers, https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/revision_history 3. Videos: insert | YouTube Data API - Google for Developers, https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/docs/videos/insert 4. YouTube API Upload Private: Your Script Worked. The Audit Is Why, https://noobclaw.com/blog/youtube-api-upload-private-2026/ 5. Using Youtube Data API makes my videos private on upload, https://stackoverflow.com/questions/64079139/using-youtube-data-api-makes-my-videos-private-on-upload 6. YouTube Data API Upload Guide 2026: Quota, Keys, Shorts - PostZen, https://www.postzen.dev/blog/youtube-data-api-upload 7. YouTube Data API - Errors - Google for Developers, https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/docs/errors 8. Comments - Issue Tracker - Google, https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/467177762 9. Resumable Uploads | YouTube Data API - Google for Developers, https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/guides/using_resumable_upload_protocol 10. Upload file data | Google Drive, https://developers.google.com/workspace/drive/api/guides/manage-uploads 11. Resumable Media Upl